:             \\\"uses_local\\\": [],\\n157:             \\\"objects\\\": [\\n158:               \\\"a\\\",\\n159:               \\\"c\\\",\\n160:               \\\"0\\\"\\n161:             ],\\n162:             \\\"produces\\\": [\\n163:               {\\n164:                 \\\"id\\\": \\\"F001\\\",\\n165:                 \\\"statement\\\": \\\"c=a.\\\",\\n166:                 \\\"objects\\\": [\\n167:                   \\\"a\\\",\\n168:                   \\\"c\\\"\\n169:                 ],\\n170:                 \\\"assumptions\\\": [],\\n171:                 \\\"binders\\\": []\\n172:               }\\n173:             ],\\n174:             \\\"introduces\\\": [],\\n175:             \\\"discharges\\\": []\\n176:           },\\n177:           {\\n178:             \\\"id\\\": \\\"S002\\\",\\n179:             \\\"text\\\": \\\"N001 gives b=a; equality symmetry gives a=b. F001 gives c=a, hence c=b by substitution. Substituting the definition c=a+0 yields a+0=b.\\\",\\n180:             \\\"uses\\\": [\\n181:               \\\"N001\\\"\\n182:             ],\\n183:             \\\"uses_local\\\": [\\n184:               \\\"F001\\\"\\n185:             ],\\n186:             \\\"objects\\\": [\\n187:               \\\"a\\\",\\n188:               \\\"b\\\",\\n189:               \\\"c\\\",\\n190:               \\\"0\\\"\\n191:             ],\\n192:             \\\"produces\\\": [],\\n193:             \\\"introduces\\\": [],\\n194:             \\\"discharges\\\": []\\n195:           }\\n196:         ],\\n197:         \\\"applications\\\": []\\n198:       }\\n199:     ]\\n200:   }\\n201: }\\n202: ```\\n203: \\n204: ## Local existence before choice\\n205: \\n206: A `definition` introduces an explicitly given expression; an `arbitrary` local\\n207: is universally fixed. Neither silently grants an existence theorem. A `witness`\\n208: requires a direct input or a prior local F establishing its existence.\\n209: \\n210: For example, after an actual argument has proved `exists b,